 "reading_outcome": "the budget SHRINKS. On 8 of the 9 layouts that carry at least 7 non-overflow bodies, the spacing at 0.5 admits FEWER than 7 — typically 5 or 6, and 4 on LV03. The cap of seven is reached on exactly ONE layout (LV10, whose spacing-only capacity is 7). At 0.3 the budget binds on 8 layouts and the spacing on 3; at 0.5 the spacing binds on 8 of 9 and the budget on 1. So by §11's own precedence rule — the spacing wins and the budget shrinks — A-G4's cap of seven was set against the 0.3 the pin bounds at, NOT against the 0.5 the record attributes to R23. The effective cap at 0.5 is 5 to 6.",
